# CRV (Conditionally Relevant Variable) Checking in lego-osek-master

## What is a CRV check?

A **Conditionally Relevant Variable (CRV)** check answers the question:

> *"Can a single-bit upset (SEU) in variable **V** cause the system to violate safety property **P** when it wouldn't have violated **P** without the upset?"*

If **yes** → the variable is **conditionally relevant** (CRV) to that property.
If **no** → the variable is **not** CRV; a single-bit flip in it cannot, on its own, break the property.

All CRV work lives under [cbmc_touch_edc/](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc).

---

## System Under Test

The controller is [nxtgt.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/nxtgt.c) — an OSEK-based LEGO NXT "GT car" with:

- **Touch sensor** on port S4: reads pressed (1) / not-pressed (0).
- **`EDC_flag`** (Electronic Differential Control): toggled on a *rising edge* of the touch sensor.
  ```c
  // nxtgt.c lines 100-104
  if (touch_sensor == 1 && touch_sensor_state == 0) {
      EDC_flag = ~EDC_flag + 1;   // toggle between EDC_ON(-1) and EDC_OFF(1)
  }
  touch_sensor_state = touch_sensor;
  ```
- **`touch_sensor_state`**: edge-tracking variable that remembers the previous touch reading.

The three internal variables under CRV analysis are:

| # | Variable | Macro | Description |
|---|----------|-------|-------------|
| 1 | `rv_touch_input` (touch sensor reading) | `SEU_TARGET=1` | The raw sensor value fed to the controller |
| 2 | `EDC_flag` | `SEU_TARGET=2` | The flag that controls differential steering |
| 3 | `touch_sensor_state` | `SEU_TARGET=3` | The edge-tracker that detects rising edges |

---

## Safety Property: P7

P7 is defined in the Copilot spec ([TouchEdcMon.hs](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/TouchEdcMon.hs)):

```haskell
let touchRises  = fr_touch && not prevTouch      -- rising edge
let touchSteady = fr_touch == prevTouch           -- no edge
let edcToggles  = fr_edc_flag /= prevEdc          -- EDC changed

let p7_body = (not touchRises || edcToggles)      -- G(touch rises → EDC toggles)
           && (not touchSteady || not edcToggles)  -- G(touch steady → EDC unchanged)
let p7 = first || p7_body                         -- skip the very first sample
```

In plain English:

> **P7:** *Globally, EDC_flag toggles **if and only if** the touch sensor has a rising edge.*

- If touch rises → EDC must toggle.
- If touch is steady → EDC must **not** toggle.

The first step is always skipped (no previous values yet).

---

## Architecture of the CRV Check

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["TouchEdcMon.hs<br/>(Copilot spec)"] -->|runhaskell| B["touch_edc_mon.c/h<br/>(generated monitor)"]
    B --> C["touch_edc_mon_orig_wrap.c<br/>(#define step → touch_edc_step_orig)"]
    B --> D["touch_edc_mon_seu_wrap.c<br/>(#define step → touch_edc_step_seu)"]
    C --> E["trace_touch_edc.c<br/>(p7_publish, violation latches,<br/>monitor reset/query)"]
    D --> E
    E --> F["harness_crv.c<br/>(main: runs original + SEU,<br/>asserts violation_orig == violation_seu)"]
    F --> G["nxtgt.c<br/>(TaskControl — controller under test)"]
    F --> H["stubs_cbmc.c<br/>(deterministic sensor/motor stubs)"]
    G --> H
    F -->|CBMC| I{"main.assertion.1<br/>violation_orig == violation_seu"}
    I -->|SUCCESS| J["NOT CRV"]
    I -->|FAILURE| K["CRV"]
```

### Key components

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| [TouchEdcMon.hs](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/TouchEdcMon.hs) | Haskell Copilot spec that defines property P7. `runhaskell` generates `touch_edc_mon.c/.h`. |
| [touch_edc_mon.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/touch_edc_mon.c) | Generated C monitor. Tracks stream history (`s0`, `s1`, `s2`) and calls `touch_edc_violation()` when the guard fires. |
| [touch_edc_mon_orig_wrap.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/touch_edc_mon_orig_wrap.c) / [touch_edc_mon_seu_wrap.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/touch_edc_mon_seu_wrap.c) | Preprocessor wrappers that `#include` the same monitor code but rename `step()` to `touch_edc_step_orig()` / `touch_edc_step_seu()` (and likewise for `touch_edc_violation`). This gives two independent monitor instances. |
| [trace_touch_edc.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/trace_touch_edc.c) | Glue code: defines the Copilot externs (`fr_touch`, `fr_edc_flag`), violation latches (`p7_violation_orig/seu`), reset/query functions, and `p7_publish()`. |
| [harness_crv.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/harness_crv.c) | **The main CRV harness.** Runs the controller twice and compares monitor outcomes. |
| [stubs_cbmc.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/cbmc_touch_edc/stubs_cbmc.c) | Deterministic stubs for OSEK/nxtOSEK APIs (motors return 0, BT returns zeros, touch returns `rv_touch_input`). |
| [nxtgt.c](file:///home/mohammed-ibrahim/Downloads/Work/PE_RE/Software_Testing/AutomatedStaticVerificationSystem/lego-osek-master/nxtgt.c) | The actual controller; compiled with `-DRV_MONITOR` to expose `rv_get/set_EDC_flag()` and `rv_get/set_touch_sensor_state()` accessors. |

